## Hands-on Demo

### Step 1: Create custom script

```bash
nano hello.sh
```

![hello.sh containing echo Hello World](adv_images/embed_p13_38.png)

```bash
echo "Hello World"
```

### Step 2: Run Script

```bash
chmod u+x hello.sh
./hello.sh
```

![Terminal: Hello World output](adv_images/embed_p13_39.png)

### Try running directly (without `./`)

```bash
hello.sh
```

![Terminal: hello.sh: command not found](adv_images/embed_p13_40.png)

### Add Current Directory to PATH

```bash
export PATH=$PATH:$(pwd)
hello.sh
```

![Terminal: Hello World after adding to PATH](adv_images/embed_p13_41.png)

---

## Temporary vs Permanent PATH

**Temporary** (lost after logout):

```bash
export PATH=$PATH:$(pwd)
```

**Permanent** (add to `.bashrc`):

```bash
export PATH=$PATH:$(pwd)
source ~/.bashrc
```

